cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Fire and pre-fire biomass in the Beni savanna–forest mosaic: a replication of Staver, Archibald & Levin (2011) on WGS84 HEALPix"
abstract: >-
  Replication of Staver, Archibald & Levin (2011, Science), who found that at
  intermediate rainfall (1000–2500 mm) tree cover is bimodal and only fire
  separates savanna from forest. ESA CCI Biomass v7.0 (2023), ESA Fire_cci SYN
  v1.1 (2024) and CHELSA bio12 are binned onto HEALPix depth 11 on the WGS84
  ellipsoid with healpix-connector for the Beni region of Bolivia (10,344 cells).
  The share of land burned in 2024 falls with pre-fire above-ground biomass
  (Spearman -0.38) and within each rainfall tercile. Outcome: partially
  supported (one region, one fire year, associational). Includes a Snakemake
  pipeline, jupytext notebooks, an RO-Crate and a FORRT nanopublication chain.
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
